s by though  it'll just become even harder to  challenge tsmc so maybe that you will  bite the bullet but we'll just have to  wait and see  while tsmc is no doubt a monopoly it  could be argued that tsmc has thus far  been an ethical monopoly they haven't  voluntarily jacked up prices or slowed  down innovation or been involved in any  sort of corruption even though all of  these would have been super easy given  their influence and control tsmc is  actually extremely strict about ethics  and integrity just a few months ago they  fired seven employees for leaking  information about apple's upcoming chips  since morris founded tsmc the company  has centered around four core values  which include integrity commitment  innovation and customer trust  while these sounds super cliche tsmc's  history over the past 34 years has shown  that tsmc has indeed upheld these values  i mean just take a look at how nvidia  ceo jensen huang talks about tsmc  because i think that moore's  his career  his philosophies  tsmc  its strategies  its core values  is absolutely  a study  in industrial revolution  there is no question about it hearing  that i think it's pretty clear that the  world's biggest companies don't work  with dsmc because they have to but  because they want to and as long as  that's the case maybe the tsmc monopoly  isn't all that bad do you guys think  that something has to be done about tsmc  comment that down below also drop like  if you're grateful for tsmc's chips and  of course consider joining our discord  community to suggest future video ideas  and consider subscribing and see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you


